values ('f1a2b3c4-5d6e-4a01-8b01-2c3d4e5f6a11', 'sociology-of-religion', 'Sociology of Religion', 'This course studies religion as a social institution, cultural system, set of practices, source of identity, field of power, and site of social change. Students learn classical and contemporary theories, empirical research methods, and major debates about secularization, pluralism, inequality, politics, globalization, media, conflict, and public life. The syllabus covers core Sociology of Religion topics, then expands them into a more granular upper-division course with research literacy and a capstone case-study component.');

