so creating spaces for agency and reform."}]}, {"id": "1a58a8bb-6dfa-4cff-8306-b343c513fded", "type": "topic", "title": "Religion, Politics, and Public Life", "description": "Explores how religious actors, identities, institutions, and moral vocabularies shape law, elections, public policy, civic life, and social movements.", "children": [{"id": "d860dfe8-c1f7-4304-8a22-e2deb3cbe736", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Religion and the state", "children": [{"id": "dffee339-4c4e-4d27-a669-29a0efd15467", "type": "concept", "title": "Establishment"}, {"id": "bb82a569-3d20-4a25-8114-04a41909e7ac", "type": "concept", "title": "Free exercise"}, {"id": "92ca2682-bc28-47a6-aab2-409ba2cfea46", "type": "concept", "title": "Laicite"}, {"id": "36cea255-793f-48c8-99b7-f32c286be656", "type": "concept", "title": "State churches"}, {"id": "141f8938-9b68-48a6-bd0e-6e0cf73df943", "type": "concept", "title": "Religious freedom"}, {"id": "e5cab573-f7c1-4411-864e-5e77f912489c", "type": "concept", "title": "Blasphemy law"}, {"id": "805700fe-a92c-49b5-8d70-1d07c846c6a5", "type": "concept", "title": "Minority rights"}], "description": "Students compare institutional arrangements that regulate religion's public role and religious freedom."}, {"id": "51cfd28d-33b7-49aa-870c-92c9080f97d1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Religion and political behavior", "children": [{"id": "69088d76-3eac-4c46-9c5b-5a4e6bc7fb2b", "type": "concept", "title": "Voting blocs"}, {"id": "fe5b39dd-5cc3-4480-8dc4-d95d2c6a1f67", "type": "concept", "title": "Issue publics"}, {"id": "369663a7-5afc-40bc-9ad5-bb456ab513c3", "type": "concept", "title": "Religious nationalism"}, {"id": "cb1ca2bd-58a5-478f-9676-2c8460e809c0", "type": "concept", "title": "Moral politics"}, {"id": "b3242f1b-ce7c-4c68-99a3-90a88917e993", "type": "concept", "title": "Public opinion"}, {"id": "e3fba673-d48a-4145-8ab7-316b950ddac1", "type": "concept", "title": "Political polarization"}], "description": "This subtopic connects affiliation, attendance, theology, race, class, region, and party politics."}, {"id": "7078d600-452d-4487-907d-9246d9185518", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Faith-based activism and social movements", "children": [{"id": "36215e5a-e1fc-4f2d-b8ea-6f30f938e0b0", "type": "concept", "title": "Civil rights"}, {"id": "8393498a-33bf-4688-8f5d-849032a23045", "type": "concept", "title": "Abolition"}, {"id": "b933c001-25bc-4c83-afa4-4aabd4fbe4fa", "type": "concept", "title": "Anti-war activism"}, {"id": "509753bc-4357-408c-b23e-221c432979b7", "type": "concept", "title": "Anti-abortion movements"}, {"id": "dfa0cd83-bee9-4fdc-9767-cd4b5ee8832d", "type": "concept", "title": "Environmental justice"}, {"id": "3a600614-fbce-41fd-8fb7-cc3d3f1876aa", "type": "concept", "title": "Interfaith coalitions"}], "description": "Students see religion as a mobilizing force in both emancipatory and exclusionary movements."}]}, {"id": "2336a186-bd08-4213-a602-c5edd452d43d", "type": "topic", "title": "Secularization, Pluralism, and Religious Change", "description": "Introduces major debates over whether modern societies become less religious, differently religious, more plural, or more polarized.", "children": [{"id": "99ab8a58-aa27-4567-ad59-29f05c9dbfc4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Secularization theories", "children": [{"id": "70f66b27-9c6c-4ff7-8745-e6dba705b6b2", "type": "concept", "title": "Differentiation"}, {"id": "dd7ed309-5083-440c-999b-1e96cf90e4fd", "type": "concept", "title": "Privatization"}, {"id": "e37d2c98-55df-4cc0-ad5d-5b17c2ac8af4", "type": "concept", "title": "Decline thesis"}, {"id": "d6c687d1-e8ef-4b7d-8683-3fd6c1716dbd", "type": "concept", "title": "Disenchantment"}, {"id": "6f6fd36d-e30a-4470-8924-2bfd163d0a2f", "type": "concept", "title": "Multiple secularities"}, {"id": "bfab1abf-0019-4b5f-bddd-3a0b1efa2ca8", "type": "concept", "title": "Post-secularity"}], "description": "Students learn the difference between declining belief, declining participation, institutional differentiation, and privatization."}, {"id": "9bb70032-f94a-4ba3-88ac-d64a41a720de", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Religious pluralism", "children": [{"id": "ffeab972-c42c-4cf4-8b17-c201d6bb1133", "type": "concept", "title": "Denominational pluralism"}, {"id": "2f53b007-fd33-4d51-b11f-1fcd06b69382", "type": "concept", "title": "Interfaith engagement"}, {"id": "7cc984f9-a765-4fb8-a7f3-b820689fb6fb", "type": "concept", "title": "Religious diversity"}, {"id": "28b93918-2472-4c98-8fb6-6b1871969d15", "type": "concept", "title": "Tolerance"}, {"id": "600f4b03-fc97-494f-a216-7fd77ec6b52c", "type": "concept", "title": "Assimilation"}, {"id": "77ea2e0e-ee0e-46f9-afb9-9549976518a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Boundary negotiation"}], "description": "This subtopic examines how diversity reshapes tolerance, competition, identity, conflict, and public norms."}, {"id": "e5745ffd-d489-44f3-9333-52cd3e839fbd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Nones, atheism, and spiritual but not religious", "children": [{"id": "568b17f6-1cd7-4e0e-a88b-3433bfd1f063", "type": "concept", "title": "Nones"}, {"id": "b0363ed9-dedc-4c38-b9bd-2e1249df5b59", "type": "concept", "title": "Atheism"}, {"id": "d0cd4121-7e5c-4d7f-82e9-2de51fa98a92", "type": "concept", "title": "Agnosticism"}, {"id": "9f7e5a59-4698-4f03-8046-8214c087a07d", "type": "concept", "title": "Spiritual but not religious"}, {"id": "3cf4df3e-4cef-48bf-b106-0e173afd2097", "type": "concept", "title": "Disaffiliation"}, {"id": "1c101510-3bf4-447b-887e-495ba3f2b79d", "type": "concept", "title": "Moral individualism"}], "description": "Students analyze disaffiliation as a complex category involving belief, belonging, politics, distrust, and generational change."}]}, {"id": "611354a5-213b-4a24-8557-71f016c5ca54", "type": "topic", "title": "American Religious Landscape", "description": "Uses the United States as a focused case for pluralism, immigration, racial formation, denominational change, civic religion, and religious politics.", "children": [{"id": "850c6a35-2038-4a9e